    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Test Evaluation and Confusion Analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "The baseline CNN achieved an overall test accuracy of **55.20%**, correctly\n",
        "classifying **138 out of 250 test images**. The macro-average and weighted-average\n",
        "F1-scores are both approximately **0.5526**. These values are equal because the\n",
        "test dataset is balanced, with five images for each of the 50 classes.\n",
        "\n",
        "The best-performing classes included `BATTERY`, `PRESSURE PLATE`, and\n",
        "`RADIATOR FAN`, each reaching an F1-score of approximately **0.8889**.\n",
        "However, performance varied considerably between classes, and `LEAF SPRING`\n",
        "was not correctly identified in the test set.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Top-3 Most Confused Class Pairs\n",
        "\n",
        "#### 1. IGNITION COIL vs OIL PRESSURE SENSOR\n",
        "\n",
        "These components have similar compact and cylindrical shapes. The displayed\n",
        "examples contain dark or metallic bodies, connector-like elements, threaded\n",
        "sections, and isolated white backgrounds. The model may therefore focus on\n",
        "their similar local geometry rather than on the structural details that\n",
        "distinguish the two components.\n",
        "\n",
        "#### 2. RADIATOR HOSE vs SPARK PLUG\n",
        "\n",
        "The confused radiator hose images contain elongated tubular shapes, circular\n",
        "openings, and strong local edges. Because the images are tightly cropped, the\n",
        "model may focus on these cylindrical details instead of recognizing the overall\n",
        "flexible shape of a radiator hose.\n",
        "\n",
        "#### 3. BRAKE CALIPER vs BRAKE ROTOR\n",
        "\n",
        "Brake calipers and brake rotors frequently appear together as part of the same\n",
        "braking assembly. The displayed examples share red or orange metallic surfaces,\n",
        "circular brake components, and similar surrounding visual context. The model\n",
        "may therefore rely on color and shared brake-system features instead of\n",
        "isolating the specific component.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Conclusion\n",
        "\n",
        "The classification report and confusion matrix show that accuracy alone does\n",
        "not fully describe the model's performance. Some classes are recognized\n",
        "reliably, while visually similar components remain difficult to distinguish.\n",
        "\n",
        "The baseline model achieved strong performance on the training set but showed\n",
        "substantially weaker generalization on validation and test images. The following\n",
        "regularization experiment evaluates whether data augmentation and Dropout can\n",
        "reduce this overfitting."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "xVW1meLO2wKQ"
      },
      "id": "xVW1meLO2wKQ"
    },
