    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Baseline vs Regularized Model\n",
        "\n",
        "The baseline CNN achieved a test accuracy of **55.20%**, while the regularized\n",
        "model achieved **32.00%** after the same 15 training epochs. Therefore, the\n",
        "regularized model decreased test accuracy by **23.20 percentage points**,\n",
        "corresponding to 58 fewer correctly classified test images.\n",
        "\n",
        "The baseline model showed severe overfitting. Its training accuracy reached\n",
        "**98.50%**, while its validation accuracy reached **54.80%**. The training loss\n",
        "decreased to **0.0482**, while the validation loss increased to **4.9516**.\n",
        "\n",
        "The regularized model behaved differently. At epoch 15, it achieved a training\n",
        "accuracy of **29.01%**, a validation accuracy of **36.80%**, a training loss of\n",
        "**2.5530**, and a validation loss of **2.3628**.\n",
        "\n",
        "The validation accuracy being higher than the training accuracy is expected.\n",
        "During training, data augmentation makes the input images more difficult and\n",
        "Dropout temporarily disables part of the model's activations. These operations\n",
        "are inactive during validation and testing.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Did augmentation help?\n",
        "\n",
        "The combination of data augmentation and Dropout reduced the severe overfitting\n",
        "observed in the baseline model. However, it also made learning substantially\n",
        "slower, and the model showed signs of underfitting after only 15 epochs.\n",
        "\n",
        "Therefore, the regularization configuration did not improve test accuracy within\n",
        "the fixed 15-epoch comparison. The selected Dropout rates may be too restrictive,\n",
        "or the regularized model may require additional training to learn useful visual\n",
        "features."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "g3cIEwZMNnWX"
      },
      "id": "g3cIEwZMNnWX"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Additional Experiment: Extended Training\n",
        "\n",
        "The regularized model was still learning at the end of the fixed 15-epoch\n",
        "experiment. Therefore, an additional experiment continues training the same\n",
        "model for up to 40 total epochs.\n",
        "\n",
        "Early stopping is used to stop training when the validation loss no longer\n",
        "improves. ReduceLROnPlateau decreases the learning rate when progress slows,\n",
        "allowing the optimizer to make smaller and more precise weight updates.\n",
        "\n",
        "This experiment is reported separately because the official baseline comparison\n",
        "uses the same fixed number of 15 epochs for both models."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "qyaw18ANgJOf"
